# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD is a boot wrapper (/boot.sh) that starts named in the
# BACKGROUND (self-daemonized, no `-g`), polls until :53 answers, then execs
# `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the resolver is ALREADY RUNNING with the open-recursion config when the
#     agent starts, which is what makes the "edited allow-recursion but never
#     reloaded named" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity` (tini reaps named), so an `rndc reload` or a
#     named restart cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RELOAD/RESTART named (rndc reload), not
# merely start it if absent - it is already up with the vulnerable configuration.
